# MovieMind front-end environment.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and edit. `.env` is also read by Vite;
# `.env.local` is the right choice for machine-specific values.
#
# Every variable here is read in exactly one place: `src/config.ts`. Nothing in
# `src/` reads `import.meta.env` directly, so this file plus `config.ts` is the
# complete list of ways this app can be pointed somewhere.

# Origin of the MovieMind API, with no trailing slash.
#
# Leave it UNSET for the default, which is what you want in development: the app
# then requests relative paths like `/api/v1/movies/search`, which the Vite dev
# proxy forwards to the backend (see BACKEND_ORIGIN below). Relative paths also
# mean the app does not depend on the backend's CORS allowlist, so it keeps
# working unchanged behind a reverse proxy or on a different port.
#
# Set it only when the API is served from a different host than the built
# front-end, e.g. `https://api.example.test`. If you set it, that origin must
# be in the backend's `cors_origins` allowlist - the backend allows four
# explicit localhost origins and no wildcard, so a typo here surfaces as a CORS
# error in the console rather than a visible message.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.test
